cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use CRAIC in your research, please cite it."
title: "CRAIC: Conserved-Region Alignment by Iterative Convergence"
abstract: >-
  CRAIC is a desktop multiple sequence alignment workbench focused on alignment
  uncertainty: it surfaces per-column and per-residue reliability, multi-aligner
  disagreement, and posterior homology, and supports interactive curation,
  codon/amino-acid views, annotations, and masking.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: McInerney
    given-names: James
repository-code: "https://github.com/mol-evol/craic"
url: "https://mol-evol.github.io/craic/"
license: MIT
version: 0.5.1
